{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1407731-companion-out-to-public","id":1407731,"title":"Companion out to public!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-12T11:18:27-07:00","id":1407731,"title":"Companion out to public!","content":"The Scion 2e Companion: Mysteries of The World is out on Drivethru. It\u2019s super good I especially recommend reading the Yazata section!<br /> Link to store page:<a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/315311/Mysteries-of-the-World-The-Scion-Second-Edition-Companion\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...tion-Companion</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T12:14:12-07:00","id":1407747,"title":"","content":"<b>IT MUST BE MINE!!!</b><br /> <br /> (And so it is. Now I just have to camp out next to my mail box until the hardcopy comes.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 08-12-2020, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T17:12:04-07:00","id":1407818,"title":"","content":"Already ordered mine.\ud83d\ude01","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T12:40:00-07:00","id":1408220,"title":"","content":"So to pick up a talk that was proceeding in another thread about the Companion...<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> - I admit it's a bit tough to pin down when an identity becomes a new Mantle, and how that plays into different things, but like, Gods <i>do</i> change, even without Mantles. Some may be a bit old fashioned, some more so than others, but like I don't think a God has to spin off a new Mantle each time they decide to try a new dessert.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T13:07:31-07:00","id":1408226,"title":"","content":"The one case that we have of that happening that I know of (Ares to Mars) didn't just involve a change in Mantles; it involved a change in Pantheons. <br /> <br /> We'll have to see what <b>Scion: God</b> has to say about it; but my gut instinct is that the higher your Legend gets, the more rigid your Mantle becomes; and while <i>you</i> may change, <i>it</i> remains the same barring a massive PR campaign to change your image \u2014 and it might be easier to create a new Mantle than to change the existing one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T14:15:11-07:00","id":1408236,"title":"","content":"Dataweaver description is my way to think. The higher the legend the god is more locked on their own concept. No matter how many times his children are killed or tortured by Hera, Zeus is fated to keep spreading his seeds, until the Romans start believing he was a bit more soberane and much less horny.<br /> <br /> The problem here is, without God all we can do is imagine, as the idea of a god with multiple mantles in a single culture is available only in the Devas, and each \u201cmantle\u201d was an Avatar that evolved all the way to godhood. Following the idea, to create an entire new mantle a god would need to go all way down to Hero and climb up again in the new form (or at least send a part of himself to do that).<br /> <br /> Another option, on a more inter cultural changing, is a god that lower his legend and start dealing with another culture to create a new mantle from the new fatebinding. That option would fit on the description Neall used for the Roman gods that have many local mantles and one main mantle, in this case going to another city and building a new legend on that place, and so a new mantle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T14:16:01-07:00","id":1408237,"title":"","content":"Yeah, we know that Fatebinding gets a lot nastier and rougher as you go up in Tier. And there's probably room to debate on what or how much of a change is enough to necessitate a Mantle Change.<br /> <br /> Edit: Okay I'm not an expert on anything but I'm pretty sure that saying &quot;The idea of a God with multiple Mantles in a single culture is available only for the Deva&quot; is wrong.<br /> <br /> Like, even with the classic Theoi, there were a lot of different variations and the like, some of it regional. Like Zeus Lykaios. A form of Zeus, but also associated with the Lykaia festival, IIRC?<br /> <br /> Like, there were MANY Zeuses and many names wherein Zeus was invoked. I'm sure someone far smarter than I has a bigger list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 08-14-2020, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T15:03:45-07:00","id":1408250,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24769_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24769\" data-vbnamecard=\"24769\">Magicjohnny</a> I totally agree!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a> good point about dessert lol<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24020_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24020\" data-vbnamecard=\"24020\">Mateus</a> Luz \ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02 to your first paragraph","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T15:22:42-07:00","id":1408255,"title":"","content":"I'm very eagerly looking forward to new gods/pantheons to play with, as well as more stuff about cults, but I think I am most looking forward to getting to experiment with the setting dials and what happens when I put them in different combinations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T15:26:25-07:00","id":1408256,"title":"","content":"(Not anything to do with the companion book)<br /> <br /> Cursory reading from various myths make me think that alot of them interact in some way with the concept that the book call mantles.<br /> The thing is it makes us go back to the god-titans-primordial thing where its better to keep in mimd that mantle is a game term and each pantheon will probably have their own spin on it.<br /> I do hope the demigod+god books look at several ways to use mantles so we can have the regional/aspected mantles of the Theoi, the All is one yet all are themselves of the Deva and the &quot;you're a word in a sentence&quot; of the Netjer. (Ps i know these examples are a very reductive way to look at it but i dont have the time or knowledge to go in more detail than that)<br /> <br /> Back on the actual topic of the thread now XD<br /> What does everyone think of the art in the book?<br /> I, myself, was quite surprised at how i liked the Yazata art spreads (both traditional and modern) because i usually dont quite like the &quot;all gods in a line looking at the reader&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T15:48:42-07:00","id":1408267,"title":"","content":"The Yazata art is good, I agree. It does a good job at indicating each of the Yazata, the only one in the art that I\u2019m not sure who they are is the one with a white beard and holed hat. But I especially like the art for the additional gods, especially the right side of it. I like seeing the gods interacting with each other","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T15:57:59-07:00","id":1408270,"title":"","content":"What I means was not that there are not gods with different mantles, what I meant was that the Devas are the only ones that have stories telling how the gods gain different mantels (avatars, in the case).<br /> <br /> But the many different Zeoi (plural of Zeus would be Zei in Latin, maybe Zeoi in Greek, Zeuses in Portuguese, pick your favorite plural) is a great example of how they work, but not how they come to exist first place (other than different worshippers and different miracles performed in those places).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T16:51:13-07:00","id":1408279,"title":"","content":"Neall mentioned in a podcast that sometimes Gods may Incarnate and actively try to come up with a new spin on their Legend in some areas, which can sometimes result in a new Mantle. Or maybe a Hero could forge a similar Legend and go &quot;Yes, I am Zeus. I am your Zeus&quot; or something.<br /> <br /> Also, my favorite bit about the Yazata art is the way they show Zam in the modern spread. Advertising a bottle of <a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Zam_Zam_cola.jpg/1200px-Zam_Zam_cola.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Zamzam</a>, which a friend of mine assures me is a fairly foul drink, even if it's a funny joke. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T17:05:44-07:00","id":1408285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1407731-companion-out-to-public?p=1407747#post1407747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>IT MUST BE MINE!!!</b><br /> <br /> (And so it is. Now I just have to camp out next to my mail box until the hardcopy comes.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd get a hardcopy...but I am still waiting on some print on demand Trinity books from drivethrurpg. Temporarily holding off for now","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T20:49:59-07:00","id":1408309,"title":"","content":"So specialized Purviews makes me wonder if Athena should have Fertility as an inheritable Purview because she herself would have Olives (Fertility)...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T02:04:21-07:00","id":1408324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1407731-companion-out-to-public?p=1408309#post1408309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So specialized Purviews makes me wonder if Athena should have Fertility as an inheritable Purview because she herself would have Olives (Fertility)...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think her Purview would be limited to olives. Athena\u2019s Legend says that she specifically never wanted to have kids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T05:19:19-07:00","id":1408338,"title":"","content":"Does this mean that Oshun &quot;who is the cool water and the brass fan&quot; can have a Fresh Water Purview, a Forge(Brass) Purview, and Purviews linked to the Brass Sword that defends the home but isn't a weapon of war? I remember how much fury I got directed towards me on the old boards when I tried to give Oshun the right number of Purviews. People were furious that she got more Purviews than Odin. When I pointed out A) she's a completely different pantheon and culture and B) more people worship her now than ever worshiped Odin, the screams of rage were audible over the internet. <br /> <br /> They didn't even listen to my suggestion they go read &quot;Africa's Oshun&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-15-2020, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T09:49:45-07:00","id":1408370,"title":"","content":"Why were they furious?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T10:28:23-07:00","id":1408375,"title":"","content":"Hm, I confess to knowing next to nothing about anything (except recalling things I've learned from smarter people), so I'll ask in genuine curiosity: Is Oshun associated with Brass-the-material and the working thereof? Or would the singular Brass Sword that Defends be better demonstrated with a variation of the War Purview? Because there's probably enough Gods who go to battle to defend rather than for conquest that there's probably design space for a defensive-war focused Specialized Purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T10:45:51-07:00","id":1408379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1407731-companion-out-to-public?p=1408370#post1408370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why were they furious?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, they couldn't see Oshun as an important/impressive goddess and powerful in her own right. Or as they said it &quot;She can't be as cool as Odin!&quot; I suspected them of less worthy motives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T11:02:51-07:00","id":1408383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1407731-companion-out-to-public?p=1408375#post1408375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, I confess to knowing next to nothing about anything (except recalling things I've learned from smarter people), so I'll ask in genuine curiosity: Is Oshun associated with Brass-the-material and the working thereof? Or would the singular Brass Sword that Defends be better demonstrated with a variation of the War Purview? Because there's probably enough Gods who go to battle to defend rather than for conquest that there's probably design space for a defensive-war focused Specialized Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've only read the one book on Oshun, and she seems to always get a specific type of role. It probably eludes to her role as patroness of the numbers five and seventeen. In her culture, the numbers four and sixteen symbolize the pattern of the known world. Thus the numbers five and seventeen represent that which is vital to the pattern but unknown, the completing power. Oshun had her own form of divination which was only about what was important now. It told only about that which was already part of the world and either hidden or misunderstood. I saw it as the mystery purview in action.<br /> <br /> Iron was the goto metal in her culture, but brass had many uses because it did not rust. Weapons of war were made of Iron and used by men. The brass sword was to defend the house and represented the rights and authority of women. The brass fan brought cooling relief. <br /> <br /> Oshun was always the cool clean water that quinched thirst and cleaned wounds. Oshun is also honey, which is a sweet, a preservative, and a medicine. <br /> <br /> She was all the subtle powers that supported the world from behind the scenes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T11:19:40-07:00","id":1408388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1407731-companion-out-to-public?p=1408375#post1408375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, I confess to knowing next to nothing about anything (except recalling things I've learned from smarter people), so I'll ask in genuine curiosity: Is Oshun associated with Brass-the-material and the working thereof? Or would the singular Brass Sword that Defends be better demonstrated with a variation of the War Purview? Because there's probably enough Gods who go to battle to defend rather than for conquest that there's probably design space for a defensive-war focused Specialized Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm. Good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T12:19:08-07:00","id":1408394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1407731-companion-out-to-public?p=1408383#post1408383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> She was all the subtle powers that supported the world from behind the scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>She was the power from home, that was both the reason to live and what keep you alive, the \u201cbehind every powerful man there is a powerful woman\u201d. It may sound sexist from our perspective, but it is empowering, much like the wise woman are respected by the neo pagans.<br /> <br /> Now on Brass, brass is easier to sharp and to keep sharp if not used and weights about half of iron, but lose the cut if hit any thing that is not soft (like an armor or an weapon), so it\u2019s good to defend as you are not going to use it often and will use against an opponent that don\u2019t expect you to be capable of defense. Iron is harder and heavier, harder to forge, harder to sharp but keep sharp after breaking armor and bone, an weapon appropriate for the warrior as he will have to use it many times during war, the metal of Ogum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T03:37:35-07:00","id":1409870,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah is anyone else confused by how according to the relic charts on pg 98, it\u2019s more expensive to have to imbue Legend to gain scale, then it is to have inherent scale via converting enhancements? Like I\u2019d feel like the former should be cheaper then the latter, because you have to use a rare resource just to gain the scale, while with the latter you have inherent scale that always applies in a certain circumstance. At least I assume when the book says \u201cimbue Legend to increase the appropriate scale rank by one point for the scene\u201d I\u2019m assuming that\u2019s also referring to increasing the scale to one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24769,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","user":"Magicjohnny","date":". 08-23-2020, 06:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T07:27:52-07:00","id":1409898,"title":"","content":"Usually, when you gain scale is more than just the scale granted by the item. For example, if you have a scale 1 sword, it will cause damage as scale 1, while when you imbue legend to gain scale it would apply to attack and defense and all actions in combat in general.<br /> Also, in this part I may be wrong, but when you gain legend from imbuing it\u2019s like one of your titles, it\u2019s half your legend, while the scale gain is 1 always (small difference for heroes though).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}